ll allāh fī al-‘ālam] Strengthener of the world and religion [mu‘izz al-dunyā wa-al-dīn] Shaykh Uvays, may God preserve his realm and his power. "  "In addition to painting, calligraphy and metalwork were also forms of artistic expression under the Jalayirids. According to the Gulistān-i Hunar, a treatise on calligraphers and painters written in 1005/1596–97 for the Safavid Shāh ‘Abbās (r. 1587–1629) by Qāḍī Aḥmad Mīr Munshī al-Ḥusaynī, one of the outstanding calligraphers of Shaykh Uvays’s time was a certain Mubārak Shāh, known as Zarīn-Qalam, or ‘golden pen’."  '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1088, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 995})
